## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design real-time, multi-tenant data pipelines with correct deduplication, rate limiting, and safe cross-tenant isolation. It also probes for practical IAM scoping, dead-letter handling, and observability under burst traffic.

## Key Concepts

- Pub/Sub streaming ingestion, Apache Beam (Dataflow) processing
- Deduplication by tenant_id + event_id with windowing
- Per-tenant rate limiting using Redis
- External risk-score enrichment via internal API
- Multi-tenant BigQuery routing: analytics.tenants.{tenant}.events
- Dead-letter queues, exponential backoff retries
- Least-privilege IAM, monitoring, alerting, cost control

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-Beam-style dedup snippet
// Deduplicate by (tenant_id, event_id) using per-tenant state
class DedupFn {
  process(element) {
    const key = element.tenant_id + ':' + element.event_id;
    if (state.has(key)) return;
    state.add(key);
    yield element;
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test per-tenant rate limiting and data skew at scale?
- How would you secure Redis and ensure tenant isolation for secrets?
- How would you handle late-arriving events that would violate dedup windows?

## Why This Is Asked
